## 25. Open tensions and input contradictions — listed, never resolved

Recorded so a reviewer can see them rather than rediscover them. **This document
does not resolve any of them.**

**Five items from the previous draft are now CLOSED by the ledger repair and the
coexistence sitting, and are struck rather than silently dropped:** DR-025's stale
capture clause and DR-024's and DR-026's unnamed vector-marking clauses are now
annotated in place and named in DR-033's `supersedes` field; DR-038's, DR-042's and
DR-044's pending-status fields now name their closing DRs; and the glossary's race,
V2-status, graph-ontology and golden-vector entries have been rewritten. Two
previous items survive (5 and 6 below), and three are new.

1. **`stage11Rollout` is a V-owned parameter that no DR names.** DR-047 retired the
   race and transformed the ticket that owned it; nothing picked it up. It is the
   one row in §4's register with no V value, and it is the parameter the
   unresolved-parameter machinery is specifically built to catch. Its sibling
   `adoptionBar` is dissolved *by implication* — DR-047 removes the adoption bar,
   the matched-cost law and the promotion question — but no DR names that parameter
   either. Carried as `OD-S-01`.

2. **A ratified label may flip under a knob ratified separately.** DR-031 ratified
   **Q27 as the battery's single `LLM` row**. DR-020 knob 8 says coverage
   *"becomes a gate only after outcome data sets the threshold"* — and a gate is
   code acting on the model's answer, which under **DR-037's label law makes the row
   HYBRID**. Today they are consistent, because a diagnostic note is stored rather
   than acted on. **No DR says whether the label follows the knob when the gate
   activates.**

3. **NEW — DR-053's dual act and DR-037's value→human route are not sequenced
   against each other.** DR-037 gives Q7 a terminal route: a settlement act of
   `value` "routes immediately to a human and stops". DR-053 introduces a typed
   **dual** act for mixed questions and runs two phases instead of stopping. It
   states that it amends *"Q7's exactly-one act"*; it does **not** say what happens
   to the terminal route when the dual act contains `value` as one of its members.
   Read literally, both fire. §3.2 and §5.5 adopt the reading that the terminal
   route binds a **pure** value act only — that reading is this document's, not a
   ruling's.

4. **NEW — DR-052 changes a DR-019 value without naming DR-019.** DR-019 knob 1
   sets the stranger-test coverage rate to **auto-ratchet up on failures**, recorded
   as a V amendment. DR-052 rules that the rate **freezes at run start and the
   ratchet applies to the next run**. That is a direct amendment of DR-019's
   behaviour, but DR-052's `supersedes` field names only **DR-021**. §4 row 18 and
   §9.2 carry the DR-052 reading, since it is the later ruling.

5. **NEW — DR-049 fixes the gate order without naming the surface R9 runs on.** The
   order is now R9 → Q53 → conformance → Q51. The stranger check is therefore first,
   which implies it runs on node text, since composed prose does not exist yet. But
   the stranger law covers **every node *and* the verdict**, and the verdict prose
   is written after. DR-049 does not say whether the composed verdict is checked
   again, nor what happens if it fails after conformance has already passed. Carried
   as `OD-S-05`.

**Two notes recorded as derivations rather than contradictions.** *(a)* Q51 and Q54
are labelled `HYBRID` in §3.10 by applying **DR-037's label law** to DR-044's text,
which describes their machine and composition limbs without printing a one-word
label. *(b)* The organ↔stage table is no longer a derivation at all — **DR-056
ratified it as FINAL**, so a lens disagreeing with a stage assignment is now
disagreeing with a ruling.

