## 2. Surface-by-surface: what replaces each of the 14

All fourteen consumed surfaces from `research/01 §A`. "Replacement" is the V3
resource(s) from §1.2 that carry the same job. "Rebuild" is the interface-side data-

### VR-5 — Does V adopt this charter's PROPOSED TEST set as blocking acceptance law?

**The decision.** DR-047 gives five clauses; this charter expands them into named tests. Codex finding
9 established that the expansion is not entailed by the ruling, so those tests are proposals until V
says otherwise. **What it changes:** whether A1.2, A3.2, A3.6, §5.1's mechanisms, A4.1–A4.5, A5.1,
A5.3, A5.5 and the `measurement_lane` exemption are release-blocking or advisory. **Options:** (i) the
whole set as blocking — highest assurance, real build cost; (ii) a named subset — naturally §5.2's
fixture table plus the never-called list — with the rest advisory; (iii) none, keeping the five clauses
as V's own judgment aid. **Recommendation:** (ii). The fixture table catches the exact disease clause 4
names; the audits and drills are cheaper to add later than to unwind.

## 9. Contradictions found (listed, never resolved)

1. **The retired race is still live in the manifest.** DR-033 part 2 and manifest §12.1/§12.3 call V2
   "the race's control arm, measured end-to-end at race time", while DR-047 retires the race and DR-025
   now survives only as the reference-capture definition. The manifest rework is queued at ticket 30,
   so the pack currently reads both ways.
2. **OD-13's owner column is stale.** The manifest routes OD-13 to ticket 15's sitting, which retired
   ticket 15's premise; the spec carries the row as `OD-C-01` here instead. A reader following the
   manifest alone looks for a sitting that will never happen.
3. **Ticket 15 still names the deleted output.** Its §Settles names `spec-pack/race-criteria.md`;
   ticket 31 and the map were repaired to `quality-charter.md`, the ticket was not.
4. **Clause 4 and DR-023 pull opposite ways.** Clause 4 indicts anything shipped and not called;
   DR-023 has V ratify a fresh flag register before production, and registers naturally contain flags
   that are off. Whether an off-by-default flag is an orphan is unruled — VR-4 names the three cases
   without choosing between them.
5. **Clause 1 and DR-039 sit in tension by design.** Clause 1 makes acceptance a human judgment on
   outputs; DR-039 forbids invented measurements. Nothing forbids converting V's judgment into a score,
   and A1.3 is the charter's reading of DR-039, not a separate ruling.
6. **DR-032 is FINAL while its own bar is a proposal.** The flag must "demonstrably fire"; what that
   means measurably is still `OD-C-02` / VR-1 — a gate required and unmeasurable at once.
7. **Clause 4's evidence base is partly excluded from the defect register.** Dead checks are
   explicitly *not* in D1–D5 by V's steer (`GLOSSARY.md`), yet DR-047 clause 4 indicts that exact
   disease at code level — one behavior outside one register and inside a charter clause.
8. **The lenses pull opposite ways on G3's force.** Codex 9 requires the charter's gates demoted to
   proposals unless ruled; Grok F5 requires the blocking demo table *completed*. This revision does
   both, so that table's force is undetermined until VR-5 is ruled.
9. **DR-055's two halves do not obviously coexist.** "Standard+ tiers must execute real different-maker
   critique from day one" and "single-maker mode stays legal as labeled degraded operation wearing
   DR-014's caps" cannot both hold *at standard+* unless the degraded mode is legal only below that
   tier. The ruling does not say which tiers keep it.
10. **The pack's single closure ledger and this register disagree on size.** Spec §23 block C counts
    **2** charter-owned rows (`OD-C-01`, `OD-C-02`); this charter carries **5**, adding VR-3, VR-4 and
    VR-5. Either the spec's count is short by three, or three of these rows belong elsewhere.
11. **"Not shipped" versus "auto-activating".** §5.2's deferred rule forbids shipping code for a gate
    that cannot fire; DR-020 knob 7's hard-kill gate **auto-activates** when the quote matcher
    validates, implying its code is present and inert until then. Whether auto-activation counts as
    shipped-dark is unruled.

